course: dictionary
lesson: 16179
title: One sign, three meanings: xx
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some short signs have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words and sentences around them, tells you which one is meant. «See you Sunday, love Grandma xx» is the end of a card, so xx means two kisses.
explain: In maths, Roman numerals use letters for numbers. «Write the number XX on the board.» In Roman numerals X means 10, so XX means 10 + 10, which is 20. Capital letters and a maths lesson are your clues here.
explain: In science, XX can be the name of a pair of chromosomes. «The XX pair is usually found in girls and women.» It is the same two letters, but it is a different kind of sign. Always ask: what are the words around it talking about? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word or sign.
fact: «xx» at the end of a friendly note means two kisses, and it is informal.
fact: In Roman numerals, X means 10, so «XX» means 20.
fact: In science, «XX» is the pair of sex chromosomes usually found in girls and women.
fact: The same letters can mean different things in different subjects, so look at the clues before you decide.
exercise: «Love you lots, see you Sunday xx» What does xx mean at the end of this card? | Two chromosomes | *Two kisses, sent to show love | Two wrong answers | Twenty
exercise: «Write the number XX on the board.» What number is XX? | Twelve | Two | Ten | *Twenty
exercise: In a science lesson on genes, «XX» means what? | A Roman number for 10 | A message ending | *A pair of sex chromosomes, usually found in girls and women | A type of kiss
test: «Sam wrote xx at the bottom of the note for her best friend.» What does xx mean here? | A wrong answer | A pair of chromosomes | *Two kisses, to show love | Twenty
test: «The XX pair is usually found in girls and women.» Which subject is this sentence from? | *Science | Music | Geography | Art
exam: The sign xx can mean two kisses, twenty, or a chromosome pair. How do you work out which meaning is right? | Pick the first meaning you remember | *Read the words around it and check which meaning fits | Always choose twenty | Skip the sign and never read on
